.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt PANELTEST 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm paneltest
.Nd step the PicoCalc panel controller through register sets
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
opens
.Pa /dev/lcdgfx ,
reads the ST7365P panel controller's registers back through
.Va machdep.picocalc.panel_read ,
and draws calibration patterns while
.Va machdep.picocalc.panel_variant
selects one of the register sets compiled into a kernel built with
.Dv LCD_PANELTEST .
Other kernels refuse both variables and
.Nm
then shows the patterns under the shipped settings only.
It needs the superuser.
.Pp
Keys:
.Bl -tag -width "1-7" -compact
.It Cm n , p
next or previous register set
.It Cm 1 Ns - Ns Cm 7
pattern: text and readback, black and white edges, gray bars,
subpixel columns, 50% gray flicker, crosstalk square, scroll lines
.It Cm r
read the registers back and show them
.It Cm q
quit; closing the device programs the shipped set again
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/log/paneltest.log" -compact
.It Pa /var/log/paneltest.log
every set change and readback, appended
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sysctl 8
